1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,260
Why do I recommend going beyond lean muscle and drinking water?

2
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:09,967
You also need the big-font theory.

3
00:00:09,967 --> 00:00:11,027
What is the big-font theory?

4
00:00:11,027 --> 00:00:13,487
It means taking all your social apps

5
00:00:13,487 --> 00:00:16,233
and switching to senior mode, with the largest font.

6
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:18,133
The strong use big fonts. The weak use small ones.

7
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:21,813
Why? The weak think their eyesight and reactions are great.

8
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,513
They think one screen can handle eight group chats,

9
00:00:24,513 --> 00:00:27,093
three shopping apps, and 17 messages to reply to.

10
00:00:27,093 --> 00:00:30,093
The strong are different. They just max out the font size.

11
00:00:30,093 --> 00:00:32,413
They tell the internet: I'm old. I read slowly.

12
00:00:32,413 --> 00:00:34,633
I reply slowly. I won't take on your anxiety.

13
00:00:34,633 --> 00:00:37,233
Once you switch to big fonts, you'll notice

14
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:39,333
there is less information on the screen.

15
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:42,933
Much of what social apps push at you disappears from view.

16
00:00:42,933 --> 00:00:45,833
Seeing 20 unread messages at a glance used to feel stressful.

17
00:00:45,833 --> 00:00:50,033
Now you open it and see only six group-chat messages.

18
00:00:50,033 --> 00:00:52,773
Psychologically, you feel less anxious.

19
00:00:52,773 --> 00:00:55,593
And when you switch food-delivery and shopping apps to big fonts,

20
00:00:55,593 --> 00:00:59,033
you see fewer product recommendations.

21
00:00:59,033 --> 00:01:02,153
You want to spend less, so you buy fewer things.

22
00:01:02,153 --> 00:01:04,513
That's very useful during an economic downturn.

23
00:01:04,513 --> 00:01:07,193
Big fonts also have a hidden benefit: they lower

24
00:01:07,193 --> 00:01:08,773
other people's expectations of you.

25
00:01:08,773 --> 00:01:11,973
I use big fonts. I'm an old person. Show me some care.

26
00:01:11,973 --> 00:01:15,800
I type slowly, so don't expect instant replies.

27
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:18,880
When your boss or colleagues see you using big fonts,

28
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:21,240
many unnecessary social ties fade away on their own.

29
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:23,740
If a colleague wants to drag you to a bar or a social event,

30
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:25,600
they see your phone filled with extra-large type.

31
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:28,540
You look elderly, even clueless, so they think:

32
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:30,180
Forget it. Let's skip inviting him this time.

33
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:32,740
It triggers the principle of the happier person yielding.

34
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:34,500
That cuts down on a lot of social hassle.

35
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:38,320
Once you use big fonts, people with normal-sized type,

36
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:41,020
instant replies, and coupon-stacking strategies

37
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:43,133
will instinctively give you a little room.

38
00:01:43,133 --> 00:01:45,293
They'll assume you're old and unsuited to the rat race,

39
00:01:45,293 --> 00:01:48,367
to late-night group chats, and that you love sleeping.

40
00:01:48,367 --> 00:01:50,667
And that consumerist anxiety won't get to you.

41
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:52,827
The big-font theory pushes back against another way of thinking.

42
00:01:52,827 --> 00:01:54,567
Today's apps all want to pack their pages

43
00:01:54,567 --> 00:01:56,867
with more content and ads,

44
00:01:56,867 --> 00:01:58,427
to hook you on mindless entertainment.

45
00:01:58,427 --> 00:02:01,333
I start ordering food and end up scrolling through short videos.

46
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:03,493
They want to train you to be always online,

47
00:02:03,493 --> 00:02:07,213
always available, and always ready to spend.

48
00:02:07,213 --> 00:02:09,633
Big fonts, drinking water, and lean muscle

49
00:02:09,633 --> 00:02:11,973
are the real infrastructure for an economic downturn.

50
00:02:11,973 --> 00:02:15,433
Drink when thirsty. Sleep when tired. Get some exercise.

51
00:02:15,433 --> 00:02:17,913
Look after your health. Make the screen font a little bigger.

52
00:02:17,913 --> 00:02:20,433
Fewer sugary drinks, fewer ads, fewer replies.

53
00:02:20,433 --> 00:02:22,813
Less anxiety and fewer needs that never needed to exist.

54
00:02:22,813 --> 00:02:25,033
That's a truly minimalist life.
